record legeos.papercut.debian-control-s-build-depends-names-only/1 : papercut {
    title "debian/control's Build-Depends names only libsqlite3-dev, but the built…"
    state verified
    statement """
        debian/control's Build-Depends names only libsqlite3-dev, but the built packages link libdisplay-info, libgbm, libinput, libpixman, libseat, libudev and libxkbcommon, so ci/source-build.sh's chroot would fail at pkg-config; and cargo-deb's $auto on the development host resolved libEGL to libnvidia-gl-580, a dependency no LegeOS package should carry. Both are symptoms of building native packages on a host that is not the target release; scripts/build-in-resolute.sh is the workaround until the source build is the normal route.
        """
    observed_at git:5681cf26fb7f1616cefb5f557d0eb84208923242
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-05
}

record legeos.papercut.deploy-pinned-the-image-metapackages/1 : papercut {
    title "`lege dev deploy` pinned the archive metapackages, so apt refused every set the ISO lane built"
    state verified
    scope [ path "cli/lege/src/dev/**", path "distro/metapackages/**" ]
    statement """
        Since the ISO lane started building the eight metapackages into the build set, `lege dev deploy` pinned all 21 packages in one apt transaction — including legeos-kernel, legeos-desktop, legeos-dev-*, and both NVIDIA rows, which Conflict with each other. apt refused the whole set on the development host ("Reached two conflicting decisions", plus unmet deps that only resolve inside a LegeOS rootfs), so no deployment could happen at all. Fixed in Installer::plan: pin only the component matrix's packages, which is what verify() already checked afterwards; the metapackages stay published so the image build can resolve against them.
        """
    observed_at git:9855da2f2647f2baa7473b2dda60b20dd702a046
    about "cli/lege/src/dev/install.rs"
}

record legeos.papercut.distro-iso-build-sh-s-customize-hook-runs/1 : papercut {
    title "distro/iso/build.sh's customize hook runs inside mmdebstrap's user…"
    state verified
    statement """
        distro/iso/build.sh's customize hook runs inside mmdebstrap's user namespace, where the calling user's uid is not mapped: the ISO tree it must drop the kernel, initramfs and signed EFI binaries into looked owned by nobody and even the namespace's root could not write to it, failing with a bare "mkdir: Permission denied" 25 minutes into a bootstrap. Fixed by creating the tree's directories up front and chmod 0777 on them.
        """
    observed_at git:0417055634d59fb6c8306840a016ffd44d85f027
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-07
}

record legeos.papercut.distro-metapackages-readme-md-promised-a-distro/1 : papercut {
    title "distro/metapackages/README.md promised a distro/metapackages/build.sh…"
    state verified
    statement """
        distro/metapackages/README.md promised a distro/metapackages/build.sh that never existed, and distro/image/compose.sh silently iterated a hardcoded seed list (minimal session desktop hardware ime a11y), so dev.seed and both nvidia seeds were declared and consumed by nothing. A generator that skips inputs without saying so is worse than no generator; `cargo xtask seeds` now renders every layer and fails on drift.
        """
    observed_at git:8b284c9147b70b4f03bb7c48ec993647e2e4df31
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-03
}

record legeos.papercut.every-reported-home-field-failure-slow-lossy/1 : papercut {
    title "Every reported Home Field failure — slow/lossy typing, a dead…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Every reported Home Field failure — slow/lossy typing, a dead shutdown button, no logout — was present in a tree where cargo test, clippy -D warnings and all seven xtask checks passed. The workspace gates cover model and layout arithmetic and cannot see the input thread, the rung a control lands on, or an interface that was never registered. Work that adds a user-facing surface should not be recorded as done on workspace evidence alone; the hands-on check needs to gate the commit, not trail it.
        """
    observed_at git:e19b3524f6dacae9152e4d6b94a6d9891edee4f4
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-26
}

