record legeos.papercut.in-lege-hostd-every-fake-fakeapt/1 : papercut {
    title "In lege-hostd every fake (FakeApt, FakeSnapshotter, FakeCommandRunner,…"
    state verified
    statement """
        In lege-hostd every fake (FakeApt, FakeSnapshotter, FakeCommandRunner, FixedClock) is #[cfg(test)] inside a binary crate, so nothing under services/lege-hostd/tests/ can use them — a transaction or deployment test can only be written as a unit test in src, and the crate's one integration test (hardware_matrix.rs) only works because it reads TOML. Making the fakes a `testing` feature module, or moving the engine into a small library crate, would let the transaction pipeline be exercised from a real integration test.
        """
    observed_at git:8b284c9147b70b4f03bb7c48ec993647e2e4df31
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-03
}

