record legeos.papercut.working-the-portal-lane-the-generated-docs/1 : papercut {
    title "Working the portal lane, the generated docs contradicted themselves…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Working the portal lane, the generated docs contradicted themselves about the same fact: docs/generated/CURRENT-STATE.md:185 says the OpenURI portal does not exist, while line 857 of the same file lists OpenURI among the interfaces the backend serves. Three source comments (portals/README.md, the crate description, main.rs's module doc) repeated the second claim, so the first thing this lane had to do was prove from the installed xdg-desktop-portal binary which one was true.
        """
    observed_at git:8b284c9147b70b4f03bb7c48ec993647e2e4df31
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-03
}

record legeos.papercut.xtask-interface-baseline-prints-froze-170/1 : papercut {
    title "`xtask interface-baseline` prints \"froze 170 member(s)\" and the…"
    state verified
    statement """
        `xtask interface-baseline` prints "froze 170 member(s)" and the following `check-interface-signatures` also prints 170, but the run before it had said "170 unchanged; 2 new" and the baseline diff added 2 lines. The count in the freeze message appears to be the pre-existing total rather than the new one, which makes it look as though the addition was not frozen.
        """
    observed_at git:392bd0d8a20b8ad0b43311cfde9ad58543c942a6
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-02
}

record legeos.papercut.xtask-interface-baseline-regenerates-interfaces/1 : papercut {
    title "`xtask interface-baseline` regenerates interfaces/baseline.json…"
    state verified
    statement """
        `xtask interface-baseline` regenerates interfaces/baseline.json wholesale, so with two lanes adding D-Bus members concurrently, whichever lane freezes last captures both lanes' additions in one write — the file then cannot be committed with a single lane's path list. A per-member merge, or a check that names which interfaces changed since the last freeze, would let concurrent additions land independently.
        """
    observed_at git:3f796cf218ad2416629d9c5f793b1bf483e91505
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-07
}
